<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Federsee</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Federsee is a lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-swabia">Upper Swabia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, surrounded by the largest moor in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. The moor has preserved the remains of many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neolithic">Neolithic</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> settlements, including the Wasserburg Buchau, and is part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> of prehistoric pile dwellings around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>. The town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-buchau">Bad Buchau</a> stands beside it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/federsee.jpg" alt="Federsee" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Effi Schweizer (User:Lily) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Federsee14.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
